# Cloudflare Pages serves a matching file first and reads these rules only
# when there is none.
#
# A missing asset has to be a real 404. A device still running the previous
# release asks for a chunk this deployment no longer has; answered by the
# catch-all below, that becomes a 200 full of HTML, which _headers then marks
# immutable for a year -- and the edge serves it under that URL even to a
# later release that builds a chunk with the same name. keybear went down for
# exactly this on 2026-08-06. So every asset directory comes first.
/js/*         /404.html  404
/css/*        /404.html  404
/webfonts/*   /404.html  404
/fonts-ui/*   /404.html  404
/languages/*  /404.html  404
/layouts/*    /404.html  404
/themes/*     /404.html  404
/images/*     /404.html  404

# One page: any other path is the app, whose router lands it on the test.
/*  /index.html  200
